<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad bin Tughlaq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1325">1325</a>–<a href="/years/1351">1351</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughlaq-dynasty">Tughlaq</a> was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> from 1325 to 1351, known for ambitious but unsuccessful schemes. These included moving the capital from Delhi to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daulatabad">Daulatabad</a> and introducing token <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> currency, which led to widespread forgery. His policies provoked revolts and contributed to the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-tughlaq.jpg" alt="Muhammad bin Tughlaq" width="288" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammad_bin_Tughlaq_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
